Given two numbers b(base) and e(exponent), calculate the value of be.Examples: Input: b = 3.00000, e = 5Output: 243.00000Input: b = 0.55000, e = 3Output: 0.16638Input: b = -0.67000, e = -7Output: -16.49971Try It YourselfTable of Content[Naive Approach 1] Using Iteration - O(e) Time and O(1) Space[Naive Approach 2] Using Recursion - O(e) Time and O(e) Space[Expected Approach] Using Divide and Conquer - O(log e) Time and O(log e) Space Using Inbuilt Functions - O(log e) Time and O(1) Space[Naive Approach 1] Using Iteration - O(e) Time and O(1) SpaceThe idea is to simply multiply b exactly e times using a iterative loop.
